+### Default ref (`resolve_default_ref`, both tools)
+
+1. `git symbolic-ref --quiet --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`, strip
+   `origin/`, and require `refs/remotes/origin/<that>` to exist.
+2. Else, if exactly one `refs/remotes/origin/*` ref exists besides
+   `origin/HEAD`, use it.
+3. Else pushed is unverifiable. `souji-verify.sh` emits
+   `NOT-SAFE(pushed-unverifiable)`. `souji-vault-verify.sh` records
+   `pushed=unverifiable(no-default-ref)` and, with no other receipt, emits
+   `NOT-VERIFIED(none)`. Local `refs/heads/master` never qualifies. Fleet
+   root's remote default is whatever `origin/HEAD` names (measured
+   `origin/master` in round 1) — do not hardcode `origin/main`.
 
