+### Live-reference sweep (`count_live_refs`, both tools)
+
+The spec's `rg --basename` is not a ripgrep flag (15.2.0 exits 2). The
+installed sweep is a fixed-string content search for the basename, excluding
+`.git`, `souji-shokunin/census/**`, `souji-shokunin/tests/**`, and
+`.ufo-quarantine/**`, plus the artifact itself. Census, test, and quarantine
+hits do not count.
+
+The sweep does not pass `--hidden`. A tool `SAFE(stale)` is not actionable
+until the same command with `--hidden` also returns 0 paths. Use `-l` so the
+output is paths only; a secret-shaped hit is routed to kagi and not opened.
+`refs=unknown` (rg status > 1) is not zero.
+
+A missing sweep root counts as 0 refs (`[ -d "$repo" ] || printf 0`). Do not
+point `SHOKUNIN_ROOT` at a missing directory. A stale SAFE is not actionable
+unless the sweep root exists and is the owning repo or the fleet root; the
+evidence field does not name that root.
+
+### Worktree order (both tools; named-branch check first)
+
+1. Named branch with `git -C <owner> log --oneline <branch> --not --remotes`
+   greater than 0 → `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)`, even when the directory is
+   absent and unique-vs-`--all` is 0.
+2. Directory absent and `git -C <owner> log --oneline <HEAD> --not --all` is
+   0 → `SAFE(metadata-prune)`.
+3. Directory absent and unique > 0 → `NOT-SAFE(none)`.
+4. Directory present and dirty, or status unverifiable → `NOT-SAFE(dirty)`.
+5. Directory present and clean → `NOT-SAFE(none)`. A live worktree is not a
+   prune.
+
+Owner is the repo under `$SHOKUNIN_ROOT` or `$SHOKUNIN_ROOT/*-shokunin` whose
+`git worktree list --porcelain` names the path. The main worktree is not a
+registration.
